cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ALAS: Aircraft Layout, Analysis and Sizing"
message: "If you use this software in work you publish, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Quiroga Rodríguez"
    given-names: "Marcos"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MarcosQuirogaR/ALAS"
abstract: >-
  ALAS is a conceptual aircraft design environment. From a set of mission
  requirements it sizes and optimizes an airframe, then evaluates the result
  across aerodynamics, mass and balance, stability, structures, propulsion and
  a simulated mission. It combines vortex-lattice aerodynamics with
  Raymer/Torenbeek empirical methods, optional coupled viscous/inviscid airfoil
  analysis, and finite-element wingbox sizing, behind both a command-line
  interface and a desktop application.
keywords:
  - aircraft design
  - conceptual design
  - preliminary design
  - aerodynamics
  - multidisciplinary design optimization
  - aerospace engineering
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-29"
